From 9b2b6c0b3b47b1e9bc2f00ad7bb7a1c0b6d4a911 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SIS Kernel Bot <sis@kernel.local>
Date: Sat, 9 Aug 2025 23:59:00 +0530
Subject: [SIS][PFM v2] PROT_U_W, NX_EXEC, GUARD_UNDER/OVER + NXE boot enable +
 paging helpers

- Adds four new Page-Fault Matrix cases:
  * PROT_U_W   : present user RO page written by user (P=1,U=1,W=1,ID=0)
  * NX_EXEC    : present user NX page executed by user (P=1,U=1,W=0,ID=1)
  * GUARD_UNDER: write into unmapped page below user stack (P=0,U=1,W=1,ID=0)
  * GUARD_OVER : write into unmapped page above user stack (P=0,U=1,W=1,ID=0)
- Adds paging helpers in memory.rs as agreed
- Enables EFER.NXE once at boot
- Extends pf_matrix.rs with mappers and Ring-3 triggers
- Extends idt.rs verification table
- Extends qemu.sh harness with tests + golden strings

